> PQC=~PQ+C+PQ*C
>
> Does the asterisk * work here, in lavaan syntax?

Not the way the poster wants it to.  The colon operator is now accepted in lavaan syntax to represent a product trem:

PQ + C + PQ:C

But it only works for observed variables, not latent variables.

Diya, look into the ?indProd function in the semTools package to create a latent interaction factor from .  And read the articles in the References section of the help page to learn how it works.  Your current syntax merely posits PQC as a higher-order factor measured by 2 indicators: PQ and C, which is not what you want.

